=0A                                                &lt;p&gt;b) Wait for it to fin=
d nearby printers, then choose the=0A                                      =
              one you want to use, and select Add device. If you want=0A   =
                                                 to remove the printer late=
r, just highlight it and=0A                                                =
    select Remove.&lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A=0A=0A=0A=0A                                   =
             &lt;h3 class=3D&quot;my-4&quot;&gt;Setup a New Printer (Mac)&lt;/h3&gt;=0A=0A       =
                                         &lt;strong&gt;=0A                       =
                             1.Prepare your printer:=0A                    =
                            &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A                                =
                &lt;p&gt;Use the instructions that came with your printer to=0A  =
                                                  unpack the printer, insta=
ll ink or toner, and add paper.=0A                                         =
           Turn on the printer and make sure it=E2=80=99s not displaying=0A=
                                                    any errors.&lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A  =
                                              &lt;strong&gt;=0A                  =
                                  2. Connect your printer: Follow the instr=
uctions that=0A                                                    came wit=
h the printer to connect it to the network.=0A                             =
                   &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A                                         =
       &lt;p&gt;=0A                                                    If you hav=
e a Wi-Fi printer, you might need to connect=0A                            =
                        the printer to your Mac with a USB cable to set up =
Wi-Fi=0A                                                    printing. After=
 connecting the printer to your Mac,=0A                                    =
                install the Mac software that came with the printer and=0A =
                                                   use the printer=E2=80=
=99s setup assistant to connect the printer=0A                             =
                       to your Wi-Fi network. After setting up, you can=0A =
                                                   disconnect the cable fro=
m your printer and Mac and the=0A                                          =
          printer should remain connected to the Wi-Fi network.=0A         =
                                       &lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A                          =
                      &lt;strong&gt;=0A                                          =
          3. Add the printer to your list of available printers:=0A        =
                                        &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A                    =
                            &lt;p&gt;=0A                                         =
           Choose Apple menu &gt; System Settings, then click Printers=0A     =
                                               &amp; Scanners in the sidebar. (=
You may need to scroll=0A                                                  =
  down.)&lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A                                                &lt;strong&gt;=
=0A                                                    4. When your printer=
 appears in the list, select your=0A                                       =
             printer, then click Add.=0A                                   =
             &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A=0A                                            =
    &lt;p&gt; It may take a minute or two for your printer to appear.=0A         =
